## 18. SECURITY AND PRIVACY

- Separate role-based layouts; route-level auth integration points; permission-aware menus/buttons.
- Client-side role checks are **not** authorization; say so in code comments and README.
- Never expose private student data on public pages; keep NID, birth certificate numbers, addresses and parent phone numbers private.
- Never expose password hashes or secrets; no sensitive auth data in localStorage.
- Result visibility only for published state.
- Confirmation interfaces for sensitive admin actions; file-upload validation UI (type, size).
- Audit logs visible only to authorized roles.

---

## 19. ACCESSIBILITY AND PERFORMANCE

Semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, accessible labels, focus management and visible focus rings, skip-to-content, sufficient contrast, screen-reader friendly controls, `prefers-reduced-motion`, responsive tables, optimized images with lazy loading, dynamic imports for charts/editor, no avoidable layout shift, no console errors, no broken links, no missing route pages. Public pages: metadata, OpenGraph, sitemap, robots, JSON-LD `EducationalOrganization`.

---

## 20. BANGLADESH-SPECIFIC

Bangla/English with Bangla-friendly typography; Bangla/English numerals; Bangladesh phone formatting; BDT formatting; Asia/Dhaka timezone; DD/MM/YYYY display; local academic terminology. Support Classes 6–10 with configurable groups and optional subjects; do not assume every class has the same groups/subjects; do not hardcode outdated exam names or grading policy. Official institutional information is configurable.

